SUMMARY:Online Info Session & Panel: MEng Co-op in CivMin
DESCRIPTION:👉Register here to join event \nJoin us for a dynamic presentation and panel discussion with current CivMin MEng Coop students!  You won’t want to miss this opportunity to learn more about the MEng Co-op program from Sebastian Goodfellow (Associate Chair – Professional Programs) and representatives from the Engineering Career Centre\, plus gain insight from MEng Co-op students who are currently completing their Co-op placement. \nPanelists will share their experiences + attendees will have a chance to ask questions about the program and connect directly with panelists in an engaging Q&A session. \nMeet our Panelists:\nNabin Basnet\nNabin Basnet holds a Bachelor of Civil Engineering from Tribhuvan University in Nepal. He moved to Ontario in 2024 and joined UofT’s MEng with Co-op program to build on his engineering background and get hands-on experience in the Canadian industry. He is focusing on Waterpower and the ELITE emphasis\, which lets him sharpen both his technical skills and his leadership. He is currently working as a Technical Trainee at Toronto Water division of City of Toronto. His proudest moment so far is that he and his daughter (now 5 years young) started school in Canada on the same day\, she in Junior Kindergarten and he in his Master’s at UofT and he loves that they’re learning side by side as they settle into this new chapter. She has even sat in on about 15 hours of his lectures at UofT. \n \nBahar Shahkaram\nBahar Shahkaram completed her Bachelor of Science in Civil Engineering at the University of Tehran and is now pursuing a Master of Engineering in Civil Engineering at the University of Toronto\, focusing on transportation planning and data analytics.  She chose the MEng for its practical focus\, and the co-op option sealed the decision. Her co-op is with York Region\, where she works on transportation planning and forecasting. Day to day\, that means GIS\, traffic data\, and building tools that help planners compare scenarios and make sense of the numbers.  Bahar started her degree thinking she would end up designing structures\, but ended up hooked on why people travel the way they do. \nAngela Zhou\nAngela Zhou is currently pursuing a Master of Engineering (MEng) in Civil Engineering at the University of Toronto\, having completed an undergraduate degree in Civil Engineering at the University of British Columbia. Angela is currently completing an eight-month co-op placement with the City of Toronto as a Technical Trainee on the Asset Data team within the Water Infrastructure Management division. Angela chose to pursue an MEng to explore areas of civil engineering beyond those covered during her undergraduate studies\, and accepted a co-op opportunity to gain practical\, hands-on experience. Growing up\, Angela loved spending time at the beaches along Lake Ontario. Now\, Angela gets to be part of the work that helps bring that same water into homes across Toronto through the city’s water infrastructure system!
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/online-info-session-panel-meng-co-op-in-civmin/
LOCATION:Online
CATEGORIES:Info sessions
END:VEVENT
