SUMMARY:Sustainability Office Industry Session
DESCRIPTION:Interested in Sustainability?\nJoin us for an engaging Industry Talk featuring Scott Hendershot\, Senior Manager of the Sustainability Office at the University of Toronto’s St. George Campus.\nWednesday\, November 25. 2026\n5 – 7 p.m.\nBA2155\nPizza provided – All students welcome \nRegister here \nScott leads U of T’s Sustainability Office\, driving initiatives that embed sustainability into campus operations\, decision-making\, and the student experience. With over 30 years of professional experience and more than a decade of leadership in sustainability strategy\, Scott brings a wealth of practical insight on creating meaningful and lasting change. \nAs a Professional Engineer (P.Eng.) and Sustainability Excellence Associate (SEA)\, Scott will share his perspectives on advancing sustainability in complex organizations\, lessons from industry\, and the role future engineers and leaders can play in building a more resilient future. \nDon’t miss this opportunity to learn from a sustainability leader and connect with fellow students over pizza! \nSpeaker\nScott Hendershot\nSenior Manager – Sustainability Office\nUniversity of Toronto – St. George Campus \nScott Hendershot leads the Sustainability Office at the University of Toronto’s St. George Campus\, providing strategic oversight and championing initiatives that advance sustainable change across the university and beyond. \nWorking with a team of five Project Managers\, Scott is focused on embedding sustainability into the fabric of campus operations\, decision-making\, and the student experience. His team collaborates across the institution to drive innovative solutions that support U of T’s sustainability goals and long-term resilience. \nJoining the University of Toronto in 2021\, Scott brought with him more than 30 years of diverse professional experience from the private sector. Prior to U of T\, he spent over a decade helping to develop and integrate sustainability strategies within the aviation industry\, playing a leadership role in advancing sustainability and organizational change. \nScott is a Professional Engineer (P.Eng.) and Sustainability Excellence Associate (SEA) with a deep commitment to creating practical\, lasting solutions for a more sustainable future.
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/sustainability-office-industry-session/
LOCATION:Bahen Centre Room 2155 (BA2155)\, 40 St. George St\, Toronto
CATEGORIES:Lectures, seminars and workshops
END:VEVENT
